From 9be8b979e3c4ae47608a397a33efa7abffde90bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:49:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Midi Kit: its players can be deleted while they play

The legacy Midi Kit (libmidi) has two threads working for a BMidi
object, and the destructors waited for neither:

- The run thread (BMidiStore plays a song from it, and BMidiSynthFile is
  built on that). BMidi::Stop() only asks it to stop -- it clears
  fThreadId -- and ~BMidi then waited for thread -1, which returns at
  once. The thread went on in the freed store and called the song hook
  for an owner that was gone: a crash, a double free, or a hook call
  after the delete (the old MidiPlayer's crash at quit). The thread is
  now remembered (fRunThread, in a reserved slot), and ~BMidiStore and
  ~BMidi wait for it to leave Run() (_StopRunThread()), the hook cleared
  first. Not waited for: a song hook that deletes its own player -- the
  run thread deleting its object -- and a thread that has not stopped
  within 5 s (a hook waiting for a lock the deleting thread holds), which
  gets a message on stderr rather than a deadlock. Either way the thread
  no longer writes fIsRunning into the freed object after Run().

- The input glue (BMidiGlue, BMidiPortGlue), a consumer whose thread
  calls the object's hooks. For a BMidiSynth they play into be_synth,
  and the soft synth sleeps in them until each note is due; the last
  BMidiSynth deleted be_synth under a sleeping delivery, which then
  crashed in fluid_synth_noteon(). The glues now deliver under a lock,
  and Detach() waits for a delivery in progress and drops the ones
  after. ~BMidiSynth detaches before it may delete be_synth (and keeps
  be_synth if a delivery does not end: a leak rather than a crash),
  ~BMidiStore before it frees its events, ~BMidiPort before it releases
  its endpoints, and ~BMidi in any case.

MidiPlayer's SynthBridge had the second problem as a Midi Kit 2
consumer that owns a BMidiSynth: its members go before the consumer's
thread stops. It gets the same lock and Detach(), called before
Release().

Tested with midikit_check (HaikuArmQemu, prose-tests): 16 players
deleted while they play, half of them after Stop(), and 4 whose song
hook deletes them; again on the guarded heap.

